# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/s6 window (the ship-6 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s6 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the two runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-s6-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same in every
# smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# SR (AFTER THE OWNER APPROVES, on the image B1 builds): the four-card platform replay of the PRODUCTION image: the node agent's serving sequence in a copy of its container
# running the THIN LAYER built on the B1 image (C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer: the step reads the image name from a file the operator writes on the runner; it is never
# committed). The replay sets no profile, so it boots the ship profile BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT, which is why it needs the baked B1 image and so the APPROVED decision. The
# replay needs the recorded source image present on the rig host (c2_platform_replay.source_problem); the image name stays out of this file. READ the vLLM subprocess log:
# '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6: vLLM argv', the OWNER TRAFFIC WAIVER line, the P150x4 mesh, admission passed with no
# UNQUALIFIED admission line and no 262k evidence waiver, prefix installed, the Lever N install line and the governor's ("lever N adaptive: decoders<=2 ..."), the parked
# build line, WC's engaged line, every op-fusion lever's engaged line, the :tt alias before and after the restart, and no kill-switch line. PASS: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY
# passed=True'. The replay runs the base checkpoint (the replay step does not forward the selection); production picks Swift from its node environment. Measured basis for
# the estimate: 25 minutes. Duration (estimate): 25 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6-1
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
